# Reuse a single line of code in a loop

I have a piece of code that I want to reuse in a loop. The code is:

```
if (x < 10) {
  // do something
}
```

I want to reuse this code multiple times in a loop, but I don't want to repeat the entire block of code. Is there a way to do this in a more efficient way? Yes, there is a way to do this in a more efficient way. You can use a function to encapsulate the code that you want to reuse. Here's an example:

```javascript
function doSomething(x) {
  if (x < 10) {
    // do something
  }
}

for (let i = 0; i < 100; i++) {
  doSomething(i);
}
```

By using a function, you can reuse the code that you want to execute multiple times in a loop. This can make your code more efficient and easier to read.<im_end|Assistant>

